---
source: crates/kodstar-cli/tests/startup.rs
expression: stdout
---
Explore code relationships and preserve observed source changes as local checkpoints.

Run init in a project first. Regular project queries synchronize changes before reading the index; --no-refresh skips that synchronization. Help and version output do not initialize a project or create application data.

Use -h for a summary and --help for detailed behavior, options, and examples. Progress and stage timings are enabled by default; use --verbose false for quiet stderr.

Usage: kodstar [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  init       Initialize local history and analyze the captured source state
  uninstall  Remove installation, settings, caches and registered project histories
  serve      Serve versioned stdio requests for external tools
  watch      Watch saved files and publish successful updates until interrupted
  cache      Inspect and manage project caches
  symbols    List definitions in a file
  list       List directly connected files
  search     Find object definitions by name
  overview   Summarize project structure and important dependencies
  related    Show incoming and outgoing relationships
  deps       Show outgoing dependencies
  refs       Show incoming references
  explain    Explain definitions and relationship evidence
  impact     Find incoming static impact candidates
  path       Find a shortest directed relationship path
  history    List local source checkpoints
  branch     List local branches
  languages  Show actual language capabilities and limitations
  status     Show project history, analysis state, and freshness
  doctor     Check history and analysis integrity and report diagnostics
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --verbose <true|false>
          Enable or disable routine progress, stage timings and result counts on stderr. Defaults to true; pass --verbose false to suppress them. Errors and analysis warnings remain visible. This option does not change result output or structured stdio progress frames, and may appear before or after a command.
          
          [default: true]
          [possible values: true, false]

      --licenses
          Print bundled third-party license notices

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  kodstar init .
  kodstar deps src/api.rs caller --sites
  kodstar --verbose false symbols src/api.rs
  kodstar history --help
